{
  "title": "Bagisto \u2014 eCommerce (26,874\u2605)",
  "content": "Project: Bagisto\nDomain: eCommerce | Scale: large | Stars: 26,874\nProblem: Bagisto is an open-source Laravel eCommerce platform that helps businesses quickly build and launch online stores without extensive development time and cost. It supports multi-vendor, multi-tenant, B2B, and headless commerce models with modern web technologies.\nTarget users: Small to large e-commerce businesses, Multi-vendor marketplace operators, B2B commerce enterprises, Developers building custom storefronts, NFT and blockchain-based marketplace creators\nCore features: Multi-vendor and multi-tenant marketplace support; Headless commerce API for decoupled frontends; B2B and B2C e-commerce capabilities; Product catalog with attributes and variants; Order and payment processing; Multi-language and localization support; Blockchain and NFT marketplace integration\nIntegrations: Payment gateways (multiple providers supported), Shipping providers, Email services, Third-party APIs via Laravel ecosystem\nTech stack: Vue.js with TypeScript, Blade templating + Laravel (PHP framework) + Relational database (MySQL/PostgreSQL compatible) + Docker support, Laravel-based deployment\nKey libraries: Laravel, Vue.js, Vite, Axios, Playwright (testing), laravel-vite-plugin\nArchitecture: monolith\nDesign lessons:\n- Modular Laravel package architecture enables extensibility through composable modules for multi-vendor and multi-tenant scenarios\n- Blade templates paired with Vue.js provides progressive enhancement\u2014works server-side for SEO while enabling rich client-side interactivity\n- Decoupled API design supports headless commerce, allowing merchants to build custom frontends independently of core platform\n- Comprehensive multi-language support (20+ languages) demonstrates i18n as first-class concern in core platform design",
